From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ejmunoz3 <ejmunoz3@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 126/126] PC5: AGS can be disabled with an environment variable
 (Wine patch 0978)

A game whose AGS_DISABLE environment variable is set in its pc5/env.txt
gets AGS_FAILURE from agsInitialize and agsInit, as on a PC without AMD's
library: the game initialises its graphics without AGS. Frostbite games
(EA Sports College Football 27) crash during initialisation with the AGS
builtin, and go further without it.
---
 docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md                        |  2 +-
 ...iver-version-for-amd-sponsored-games.patch | 21 ++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 19 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md b/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
index 736c606..a1b2c3e 100644
--- a/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
+++ b/docs/WINE_PS5_BUILD.md
@@ -188,7 +188,7 @@ before evaluating a candidate built from that cache.
 | 0975 (upstream 0986) | `ntdll`: accesses that 0974 steps over beside a protected page are counted, reads too. When a host page has had 256 of them, a write beside a read-only page is still reported there, and any other access gives the host page the union of its pages' protections, as before 0974, until a protection in it changes. Beside an inaccessible page nothing ended the stepping: Unity's Mono garbage collector (Darkwood) took about 13,000 steps a second and ran at 5 fps |
 | 0976 | `ntdll` (Mihawk OS 2085): on PS5, a boolean socket option (`SO_BROADCAST`, `SO_KEEPALIVE`, `SO_REUSEADDR` and the other boolean `SOL_SOCKET` ones, `TCP_NODELAY`) reads back as 0 or 1, as on Windows and Linux. The console's FreeBSD kernel answered with the option's flag bit (`SO_BROADCAST` as 0x20), so a program that compares the value with TRUE took a set option for unset |
 | 0977 | `win32u` (Mihawk OS 2152): `GetClipCursor` keeps the clip inside the virtual screen. In an emulated display mode (a 640x480 mode drawn letterboxed on the 1920x1080 output) the unclipped raw rect is the whole physical screen, which mapped back into the mode reached past its sides |
-| 0978 | `amd_ags_x64` (Proton's, ValveSoftware/wine, LGPL; `amd_ags.h` AMD's, MIT): AMD's GPU Services library as a builtin, answering from the Vulkan device with a current driver version, so AMD-sponsored games (Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered, The Last of Us Part II) don't take the PS5 for a missing or outdated driver; AGS's Direct3D 11 and 12 extensions go to DXVK and VKD3D-Proton. No Unix side (no libdrm on the PS5). A title overrides `amd_ags_x64` to builtin for a game's own copy to give way. The version the game was made for is read from the game's own copy only: a game that calls `agsInit` on the system directory's copy, which only Wine has (Avatar Legends: The Fighting Game), gets `AGS_FAILURE` and goes on without AGS, where the builtin had asked itself for its version until the stack ran out |
+| 0978 | `amd_ags_x64` (Proton's, ValveSoftware/wine, LGPL; `amd_ags.h` AMD's, MIT): AMD's GPU Services library as a builtin, answering from the Vulkan device with a current driver version, so AMD-sponsored games (Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered, The Last of Us Part II) don't take the PS5 for a missing or outdated driver; AGS's Direct3D 11 and 12 extensions go to DXVK and VKD3D-Proton. No Unix side (no libdrm on the PS5). A title overrides `amd_ags_x64` to builtin for a game's own copy to give way. The version the game was made for is read from the game's own copy only: a game that calls `agsInit` on the system directory's copy, which only Wine has (Avatar Legends: The Fighting Game), gets `AGS_FAILURE` and goes on without AGS, where the builtin had asked itself for its version until the stack ran out. A game whose `AGS_DISABLE` environment variable is set (in its `pc5/env.txt`) gets `AGS_FAILURE` from `agsInitialize` and goes on without AGS, as on a PC without AMD's library: Frostbite games (EA Sports College Football 27) crash with the AGS builtin and go further without it |
 | 0973 | `win32u`: on PS5, a shown window the size of the part a display mode covers (0932), but at another place on the desktop, is what frames show and where the pointer stops: DirectDraw drawing with GDI (Heroes of Might and Magic IV in 2D only) sized its window to the mode from the desktop's top left, and the centred part showed its picture cut off on the left |
 | 0979 | `win32u`: on PS5, a launch window that reads only the keyboard takes the dialog keys of 0911 (Cross as Enter, the D-pad as the arrows) as a dialog box does: Nixxes' (Marvel's Spider-Man Remastered and its other ports), a 792x447 pop-up of the class `GameNxApp` with Play, Settings and Quit, while it is smaller than the display both ways. The game's own window, which may share the class, covers the display and never gets those keys beside its controller |
 | 0980 | `win32u`: on PS5, each move, new image or hiding of the cursor also goes to `libvulkan.prx`'s `pw_videoout_cursor_follow`, so VideoOut's hardware cursor follows the pointer between presents, unless a desktop frame (the cursor drawn in) is what shows. A game that draws only when something changes (Age of Empires II HD's menus) had lost its pointer: it followed only at a present |
diff --git a/wine/patches/0978-amd-ags-x64-a-driver-version-for-amd-sponsored-games.patch b/wine/patches/0978-amd-ags-x64-a-driver-version-for-amd-sponsored-games.patch
index 4eb8c86..f9a3b2c 100644
--- a/wine/patches/0978-amd-ags-x64-a-driver-version-for-amd-sponsored-games.patch
+++ b/wine/patches/0978-amd-ags-x64-a-driver-version-for-amd-sponsored-games.patch
@@ -27,5 +27,10 @@ AGS_FAILURE and goes on without AGS, as on a PC without AMD's library:
 before, the builtin loaded itself to ask its own agsGetVersionNumber, which
 asked again until the thread's stack ran out.
+
+A game whose AGS_DISABLE environment variable is set gets AGS_FAILURE from
+agsInitialize and agsInit, as on a PC without AMD's library: the game
+initialises its graphics without AGS. Frostbite games (EA Sports College
+Football 27) crash during initialisation with the AGS builtin.
 ---
 diff --git a/configure b/configure
 index 50b8006..845ff91 100755
@@ -2224,11 +2229,11 @@ index 0000000..32b47f2
 +@ stdcall agsGetGPUInfo(ptr ptr)
 diff --git a/dlls/amd_ags_x64/amd_ags_x64_main.c b/dlls/amd_ags_x64/amd_ags_x64_main.c
 new file mode 100644
-index 0000000..3becf4f
+index 0000000..a1c2d3e
 --- /dev/null
 +++ b/dlls/amd_ags_x64/amd_ags_x64_main.c
-@@ -0,0 +1,2074 @@
+@@ -0,0 +1,2085 @@
 +#if 0
 +#pragma makedep arm64ec_x64
 +#endif
 +
@@ -3006,6 +3011,17 @@ index 0000000..383d212
 +
 +    memset(context, 0, sizeof(*context));
 +
++    /* A game whose AGS_DISABLE environment variable is set gets AGS_FAILURE, as on a PC without
++     * AMD's library, so it initialises its graphics without AGS (Frostbite: College Football 27). */
++    {
++        WCHAR val[2];
++        if (GetEnvironmentVariableW(L"AGS_DISABLE", val, ARRAY_SIZE(val)))
++        {
++            WARN("AGS disabled by AGS_DISABLE environment variable.\n");
++            return AGS_FAILURE;
++        }
++    }
++
 +    /* Without the game's own library, as on Windows, where only games ship AMD's library: the game
 +     * goes on without AGS, as on a PC without it, rather than with a version it wasn't made for. */
 +    if (!ags_version && from_system_directory())
--
2.43.0
